# Normalise line endings: LF in the repository *and* in working trees.
#
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text file to CRLF
# on checkout. That is invisible while one person works on one machine, but a
# collaborator on macOS or Linux then sees whole-file diffs on files nobody
# touched. `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf per-repo, so the working copy matches what
# is stored and no conversion happens in either direction.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. `text=auto` detects most of
# these on content, but being explicit means a corrupt asset can't slip through
# on a file that happens to look like text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
